50,3,1,talk,Mio,,"The candidates are A: Textiles, B: Light and Motion, C: Maritime Trade, and D: City Under Excavation. I like A or D.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"D has a working conservation bench, but with only one staff member in the lab, is that realistic? A seems safer.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Shion,,"B has the mechanisms people love, but D has the ""working"" element the visitors requested. I lean toward D.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"B's rigging might be too heavy for the bay, and C's loans are risky. D uses municipal finds, which are local.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Shizue,,B is a nightmare for maintenance and C is a risk for shipping delays. A and D are the only stable choices.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, would D's reconstructions be too heavy for the floor?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, as long as they aren't massive stone blocks, it should be fine. But A's textiles are very light.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, but A is just garments. D's working bench is a huge draw for the public.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, the ""working bench"" in D is a great way to use the space without needing complex, fragile arrangements.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Victoria, if the lab is backed up, having the bench in the gallery might actually help visibility and engagement.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm worried about the cost of mounts for D. But A's demonstration sessions sound lovely and cheap!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, A uses practicing craftspeople, not our internal lab staff. That solves my staffing concern completely.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Shion,,"A has the ""people working"" element and is safer than B. I can support A.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"A is light, local, and doesn't interfere with evening hire. It is the most logical choice.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Shizue,,A avoids the shipping delays of C and the technical failures of B. I vote for A.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'll go with A! It's cheerful and budget-friendly.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. A is the most sustainable for our current staff.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Shion,,I'll vote A for the visitor engagement.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Asuka,,A is the most rational fit for the building.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I concur. A is the safest path.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
